    "Subsea pressure-vessel compute, onshore seawater-cooled compute and floating offshore platforms are separate architecture classes.",
    "Module IT capacity, whole-facility electrical capacity, site grid import and renewable nameplate are different quantities.",
    "PUE comparisons require identical whole-facility meter boundary and time window.",
    "WUE claims must distinguish freshwater consumed by the data centre from seawater intake, discharge and ecosystem impacts.",
    "Seawater cooling does not imply environmental acceptability; intake, thermal discharge, biofouling, chemical treatment, plume and habitat impacts require site-specific evidence.",
    "Compute throughput comparisons require workload, model, precision, accelerator, quality, latency, availability and power boundary.",
    "Reliability comparisons require sample size, confidence interval, operating duration, failure definition, repair strategy and matched control.",
